# Prefab-Authored UI Layout

Runtime UI scripts (`*View`, HUD, overlays) must **not** hardcode layout — positions, sizes, anchors, offsets, spacing, or font sizes. Author that on the **prefab** (Unity Editor / MCP). Runtime code drives **content and state** only.

**Why:** Designers and developers tune prefabs in the Inspector. Hardcoded layout in C# silently overrides those edits at play time.

This rule applies to **runtime** presentation code. **Editor** scripts that build or migrate prefabs may set layout in code — that is authoring, not play-mode override.

## Runtime view contract

- Hold `[SerializeField]` refs to prefab children; wire in the Inspector.
- Update text, sprites, colors, visibility, interactable state, and data-bound values.
- Do **not** assign `RectTransform` layout properties for static chrome.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — play-mode layout overrides prefab edits
rowRt.anchorMin = rowRt.anchorMax = new Vector2(0.5f, 0.5f);
rowRt.anchoredPosition = new Vector2(RowCenterX, y);
rowRt.sizeDelta = new Vector2(RowWidth, RowHeight);

// ✅ GOOD — layout authored on prefab; code updates content
[SerializeField] private TextMeshProUGUI _amountText;
public void SetAmount(string text) => _amountText.text = text;
```

## Banned in runtime UI (static layout)

- `anchoredPosition`, `sizeDelta`, `anchorMin`/`anchorMax`, `offsetMin`/`offsetMax`, `pivot`, `localPosition`/`localScale` on UI chrome for baseline placement
- Layout constants (`RowWidth`, `FirstRowY`, `NameFontSize`, …) used to position or size elements
- Runtime `new GameObject(...)` + `AddComponent<Image|Button|TextMeshProUGUI|LayoutGroup>` to build screen chrome (see also `no-code-built-ui` when present)

## Allowed at runtime

- **Content/state:** `.text`, `.color`, sprite/material swaps, `SetActive`, `interactable`, toggles
- **Data-proportional sizing:** fill width/height from a **serialized** authored max (e.g. stat bar fill = `_barWidth * ratio`) — the bar track and max width live on the prefab
- **Animations:** temporary transforms during tweens; restore or let the animation end
- **Safe area / device insets:** dedicated `SafeArea` (or equivalent) components that adjust for notch/home indicator — not per-screen magic numbers
- **Layout rebuild after content change:** `LayoutGroup` / `ContentSizeFitter` on the prefab; code may call `LayoutRebuilder.ForceRebuildLayoutImmediate` when dynamic text changes size — not replace authored spacing with constants
- **Pooled/list rows:** instantiate a **row prefab** authored in Editor; bind data only — no per-row layout math in the view

## Editor authoring is exempt

`Editor/` scripts, menu items, and one-off prefab migration tools may construct hierarchy and set `RectTransform` values — that **is** how the prefab gets its layout.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] New/changed runtime UI keeps positions/sizes/anchors on the prefab, not in C#
- [ ] View scripts only update content, visibility, and data-driven values
- [ ] Dynamic lists use authored row prefabs, not code-built rows with hardcoded layout
- [ ] Layout constants and `RectTransform` assignment removed from runtime paths (not moved to "config")
- [ ] Editor prefab-build scripts are the only place that sets baseline UI layout in code
